# Frontend Testing — framework-agnostic

## Three layers
| Layer | Tool | Scope |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | jest | pure functions, reducers, selectors, codecs |
| Integration | jest + UI lib + msw | components rendered with real state container + mocked network |
| E2E | @playwright/test | full app, real browser, mocked back-end at network edge |

## What to test / not test
- Test: every component handling user input, every reducer/selector/utility, every user journey.
- Don't: implementation details, library internals, trivial passthroughs.

## MSW
- HTTP handlers in `src/test/handlers.ts` or `packages/test-utils/handlers.ts`.
- `server.resetHandlers()` in `afterEach`. Per-test overrides via `server.use(...)`.
- Default handlers = happy path; tests opt into failure modes.

## Real-time tests
- WebSocket fake in `packages/test-utils/ws-fake.ts`.
- Drive synchronously; cover connect / first / disconnect / reconnect / malformed / buffer overflow.

## Playwright
- One `playwright.config.ts` per app. Run against built preview, not dev server.
- `route.fulfill()` for deterministic flows; reserve real back-end for smoke.
- `trace: "on-first-retry"`. Screenshot on failure.
- `@axe-core/playwright` on every page-level spec.

## Coverage
- ≥ 80% on `apps/*/src/features/` and every `packages/*` library.
- Coverage is a smoke alarm, not a goal.
